# Random instances for the end-to-end check (lean/test/e2e.sh): <name>|<zeno arguments>.
# @DATA@ expands to lean/test/instances. The r* instances with a forest gap in their
# certificate exercise the converse (Theorem 4.7) and the sigma-DP bound. tree12 (12
# non-dominated cities, two forest gaps) exercises the link-forest tree DP.
r155|-n 8 -t 11 -p 2 -d @DATA@/r155.dat
r169|-n 7 -t 7 -p 4 -d @DATA@/r169.dat
r225|-n 10 -t 15 -p 7 -d @DATA@/r225.dat
r240|-n 7 -t 11 -p 6 -d @DATA@/r240.dat
r25|-n 10 -t 18 -p 8 -d @DATA@/r25.dat
r10|-n 7 -t 12 -p 5 -d @DATA@/r10.dat
r101|-n 10 -t 14 -p 5 -d @DATA@/r101.dat
tree12|-n 12 -t 10 -p 4 -d @DATA@/tree12.dat
